course: dictionary
lesson: 4354
title: Words for people who play
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Look at the word guitarist. It is guitar with -ist on the end, and the ending often names a person who does something. A guitarist is a person who plays the guitar.
explain: The sentence gives you the clue: «Many drummers and guitarists started on the recorder at school.» Drummers play drums, so guitarists must be the people who play guitars. Ask yourself who does the action, and the word will tell you.
explain: Phrases add detail. A lead guitarist is the main guitar player in a band, and a bass guitarist plays the low notes. In «a guitarist's fingertips grow thick hard calluses», the word tells you that this person plays so much that their fingers toughen up.
fact: A guitarist is a person who plays the guitar.
fact: Guitarist is a noun. Its plural is guitarists.
fact: The ending -ist often names a person who does something, like pianist or cyclist.
fact: «Lead guitarist» and «bass guitarist» are two kinds of guitarist in a band.
fact: Playing the guitar often for a long time can make a guitarist's fingertips grow thick, hard calluses.
exercise: «Many drummers and guitarists started on the recorder at school.» Who is a guitarist? | A person who runs very fast | *A person who plays the guitar | A person who cooks the school lunch | A person who sells recorders
exercise: Ella says a lead guitarist is a teacher. What is a lead guitarist really? | *The main guitar player in a band | A person who builds guitars | A teacher of the recorder | A person who sings and never plays
exercise: Which word is the plural of guitarist? | guitarist's | guitarish | *guitarists | guitar
test: «A guitarist's fingertips grow thick hard calluses.» Why would a guitarist have calluses? | Because they paint pictures every day | Because they swim for hours in the sea | *Because they press the strings hard and play often | Because they hold cold ice in their hands
test: What is a bass guitarist? | *A person who plays the low notes on a bass guitar | A person who carries the band's equipment | A person who sings the highest notes in a choir | A person who plays the drums in a band
exam: Which word means a person who plays the guitar? | guitarship | guitars | *guitarist | guitar
